  setConnCheck: 'Scheduled connectivity check', setConnCheckD: 'When on, this gateway dials every instance on a schedule and records reachable/unreachable on the data sources page. Off by default: without it, that column only updates when someone runs a batch check.',
  setConnCheckInterval: 'Interval (minutes)', setConnCheckIntervalD: 'How long between rounds. Minimum 1, maximum 1440 (one day). Changes take effect without a restart.',
  setConnCheckConcurrency: 'Concurrent dials', setConnCheckConcurrencyD: 'How many instances to dial at once. Capped at 16.',
  setConnCheckSkip: 'Three kinds are skipped', setConnCheckSkipD: 'Instances in maintenance, instances with no credentials, and instances whose last check failed on authentication. The last one guards against account lockout: Oracle locks after 10 failures by default, so an instance with wrong credentials checked every 10 minutes would lock the gateway account in under two hours. After fixing the credentials, run a manual check on the data sources page to resume automatic checks.',
  setMeta: 'Metadata sync', setMetaSub: 'Keep a local copy of remote table lists and column structures, so search need not ask production every time.',
  setMetaEnabled: 'Scheduled sync', setMetaEnabledD: 'When on, this gateway periodically logs in to every instance to read its structure. Off by default: that is a deliberate decision, not something a version upgrade should start doing on its own.',
  setMetaInterval: 'Interval (hours)', setMetaIntervalD: 'How long between full sweeps. Below 1 counts as 1; the maximum is 720 (30 days). Changes take effect without a restart.',
  setMetaConcurrency: 'Concurrent instances', setMetaConcurrencyD: 'How many instances at once. Capped at 8 — beyond that it stops being metadata collection and becomes a concurrent login storm against your own production cluster.',
  setMetaNote: 'Three things to know', setMetaNoteFirst: 'One: turning it on does not start a sweep. The clock runs from gateway startup, so the first sweep is one full interval away. To verify now, use the per-instance Sync metadata now button on the Data sources page.',
  setMetaNoteSkip: 'Two: instances in maintenance and instances with no credentials are skipped, and leave no record. So when an instance shows no tables at all, first check whether it was skipped.',
  setMetaNoteStale: 'Three: this data is a read-only copy, not the truth. Judgement, execution and export all still go to the live target — a possibly stale structure used for a decision turns fast into wrong.',
